From b6dc51733439d7f63b2da3c3a6305a6a95b319c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hank Yeomans <hank@quorra.ah.local>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:55:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 31/50] dsv4 indexer: publish prefill candidates as block-ID
 lists (recipe E34e e-i)

select_candidate_block_ids / expand_candidate_ids replace the block keep mask on
both prefill publish/consume paths. The keep mask was one byte per block of
prefix per row and the only prefix-scaling live tensor left at 512K (275 MiB at
384K, 0.5 GiB worst at 512K, 1 GiB at 1M, 2x during torch.cat; recipe E34e
e-ii). The ID list is 4 B x candidate_topk_blocks per row whatever the prefix
(64 MiB at 8192 rows), -1 padded, bit-exact to the keep path by construction.
The -1 entries scatter into a spare column (a clamp to 0 races a real block-0
pick). Decode (two_level_decode_logits) unchanged.

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a0c10b-a5f8-77fc-b238-7147d12ccf29
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
